abstract: >-
  Tooling that runs Epic Games' City Sample (Unreal Engine 5.8, both
  Small_City_LVL and Big_City_LVL) as a CARLA 1.0 driving simulator, and
  extracts the city's road network as multi-lane ASAM OpenDRIVE so it can be
  driven in any CARLA. Includes an Unreal plugin that exports Epic's ZoneGraph,
  converters that produce multi-lane OpenDRIVE with mid-block lane changes,
  road-class speed limits, traffic lights, stop signs, yield signs, speed-limit
  signs and exact reference-line crosswalks, bi-directional synchronisation
  between Epic's MassTraffic intersection signals and CARLA's traffic light
  controllers, a two-way Mass ECS bridge that mirrors Epic's traffic and crowd
  around the ego vehicle into the CARLA API while exporting CARLA actors back
  into Mass as obstacles, an out-of-the-box semantic tagger for geometry
  streamed through FastGeoStreaming and Mass visualizers, a pedestrian navmesh
  builder backed by Epic's measured ZoneGraph pedestrian lanes, and verified
  compatibility with CARLA 1.0's NVIDIA NuRec neural reconstruction pipeline.
  No Epic Games content is redistributed.
keywords:
  - CARLA
  - Unreal Engine
  - City Sample
  - autonomous driving
  - driving simulator
